    "created_at": "2019-01-09T18:46:27Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-01-09T18:46:27Z",
    "body": "Thanks for the response, @annevk. Your snippet indeed works, and without that much extra code. That said, IMHO having parallel `valid` and `invalid` events would be more elegant in some cases. (I'm not sure why, if we have one event, we wouldn't have the other?)\r\n\r\nI've mocked up a CodePen to show what I'd like to do: https://codepen.io/mark-fluehr/pen/dwqPqW?editors=1010. The important part is these lines:\r\n```JavaScript\r\nfields.forEach((field) => {\r\n  // This works\r\n  field.addEventListener('invalid', showWarning);\r\n\r\n  // This doesn't work, as it's not in the DOM API\r\n  field.addEventListener('valid', hideWarning);\r\n});\r\n```",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
