    "created_at": "2019-01-10T09:55:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-01-10T09:55:13Z",
    "body": "Because it doesn't really make sense to dispatch a `valid` event whenever we dispatch an `invalid` event today. The processing model would be quite a bit different, meaning there's no real symmetry to speak of, at which point it's not clear to me that it's a good thing to have both.",
